{
 "@context": "https://real-life.org/meta/v1/context.jsonld",
 "@graph": [
  {
   "@id": "rlnp:Spiegel",
   "skos:exactMatch": "rls:mirror"
  },
  {
   "@id": "rlnp:Mensch",
   "skos:relatedMatch": "rltp:Anchor",
   "skos:note": "Deliberately no exactMatch: RLTP has no person object, only anchors per context. This is by design (relationships never converge into a person)."
  },
  {
   "@id": "rlnp:Mensch",
   "skos:relatedMatch": "rls:profile",
   "skos:note": "The profile is the view of a person, not the person."
  },
  {
   "@id": "rls:connector",
   "skos:note": "Deliberately without counterpart in RLNP and RLTP. The connector is pure Stack construction."
  },
  {
   "@id": "rlnp:Kreis",
   "skos:note": "Converged 2026-09-18: a circle is the thing itself; the Stack constructs it as a space, the Trust Protocol as a group. A circle chooses its own form and access, and the space carries exactly that: publicly visible, open for anyone to post, or by invitation. \"Space\" in the RLNP text is a reference to the Stack space, not a term of its own.",
   "skos:exactMatch": [
    "rls:space",
    "rltp:Group"
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "rls:space",
   "skos:exactMatch": "rltp:Group"
  },
  {
   "@id": "rlnp:Sichtbarkeit",
   "skos:relatedMatch": [
    "rltp:VisibilityMode",
    "rls:mirror"
   ],
   "rl:convergesWith": "rls:visibility",
   "skos:note": "Three ways, three constructions: \"within the circle\" = RLTP private; \"mirrored\" = Stack mirror bridge; \"published\" = RLTP open is only the origin, delivery of open data needs another backend (multi-connector). VisibilityMode covers the first two only."
  },
  {
   "@id": "rlnp:Verifikation",
   "skos:exactMatch": "rltp:Enactment",
   "skos:relatedMatch": "rltp:EncounterCredential",
   "skos:note": "The act is the same; the credential is its result."
  },
  {
   "@id": "rlnp:Bezeugen",
   "skos:relatedMatch": "rltp:EncounterCredential",
   "rl:convergesWith": "rltp:Attestation",
   "skos:note": "Target: a general attestation type in RLTP (candidate: DTG Endorsement Credential). Until then only the encounter has an artifact."
  },
  {
   "@id": "rltp:Member",
   "skos:exactMatch": "rls:member",
   "skos:note": "Deliberately without a counterpart in RLNP (2026-09-18): the network knows membership only as what it must not require. Belonging to the network lives in relationships, not in lists; a circle chooses its own form and access, and membership is one of the forms the Stack and the Trust Protocol provide for it."
  },
  {
   "@id": "rlnp:Rolle",
   "rl:convergesWith": "rltp:Attestation",
   "skos:note": "A role taken on is a witnessed promise (RLNP 6.18, 8.13). Depends on the attestation type."
  },
  {
   "@id": "rlnp:Beziehung",
   "skos:narrowMatch": "rltp:Edge",
   "rl:falseFriend": "rls:relation",
   "skos:note": "Decided 2026-09-18 (for now): an RLNP relationship is broader than an RLTP edge. Two kinds: person–person is an edge from an encounter (RLTP Edge); person–agent is an edge from appointment or vouching (future attestation). Proposal to RLNP 6.2: name both kinds. Relation (Stack) links items, not people: false friend.",
   "rl:convergesWith": "rltp:Attestation"
  }
 ]
}